<% identity = Rails.configuration.x.foundation %>
<article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-md-on-surface-variant">
      Version <%= Foundation::Legal.terms_label %>
      &middot; Last updated <%= Foundation::Legal::TERMS_UPDATED_ON.iso8601 %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 rounded-md border border-md-tertiary bg-md-tertiary-container px-4 py-3 text-sm text-md-on-tertiary-container">
      Demo preview: this deployment is test-only. Review these terms with
      qualified counsel before a production launch and add the operator's
      legal name, entity type, and registered address here.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (the "Terms") are an agreement between you and
      the operator of <%= identity[:application_name] %> (the "Service").
      Until the operator is named for production, this demo is operated as
      a test preview. Questions about these Terms can be sent to
      <%= mail_to identity[:legal_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. What the Service is</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is a one-page guestbook reachable at
      https://<%= identity[:domain] %>. Visitors type a short message and it
      is shown publicly on the wall, newest first. There are no accounts,
      no purchases, and no billing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Your messages</h2>
    <p>
      By posting a message you keep any rights in its content and grant the
      operator a non-exclusive license to host and display it so the Service
      can show it on the wall. Do not post content you have no right to
      share, anything illegal, or anything that harasses, threatens, or
      impersonates another person. The operator may remove any message it
      reasonably believes violates these Terms.
    </p>
    <p>
      Messages are public. Do not include personal information about yourself
      or others that you do not want anyone to see.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>When using the Service you agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>break the law, or help anyone else break it;</li>
      <li>probe, scan, overload, or attempt to bypass security or rate limits;</li>
      <li>scrape or bulk-collect messages or other data;</li>
      <li>upload malware or content you have no right to share;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten, or defraud other people.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We may
      suspend or discontinue it, in whole or in part, at any time. The demo
      deployment is reset daily and is not a reliable place to store anything
      important.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The current version is
      always available here, and continued use of the Service after a change
      means you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about these Terms, contact
      <%= mail_to identity[:legal_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
